  volume           = {24},
  annotation       = {Describes various issues of epistemology and authority in Tibetan medicine from the fifteenth to the 20th centuries including the indigenous Tibetan debates about reconciling the tantric body with the strictly medical one (they didn't succeed). Tension between authority and perception. Story, p.90, about the Fifth Dalai Lama bringing foreign doctors to Tibet, including several Indians, one of whom, in 1675, taught cataract surgery to Dar-mo, who actually did it on the Fifth. Also, an account of the Tibetan debate about whether the Four Tantras were a Buddhavacana and/or Indian (a good thing), or whether they were a Tibetan composition, and therefore not so authoritative. Refers in f.n.27 to \cite[252--6, 477--85, 535--40]{isra-radi} on the issue of what constituted the Early Modern scientific revolution in Europe, and the issues in Europe about perception and scripture.},
