  annotation       = {03.7.29 p.36 In trying to get her informants to draw the dosas or dhatus, Langford misses the fact that such drawings form no part of the tradition, and never appear in manuscripts. In spite of having read Zimmermann, she seems not to have understood deeply the profoundly linguistic turn of the ayurvedic tradition, that it really, really is a discourse, and does not willingly lend itself to visual representation. In refusing to provide her with the diagram she requested, Langford's informant was cleaving to a deep truth within his tradition, the truth that these ayurvedic categories are not visual, but narrative objects. Ayurveda as a response to urbanisation. Source? http://login.ezproxy.library.ualberta.ca/login?url=https://read.dukeupress.edu/books/book/744/Fluent-Bodies-Ayurvedic-Remedies-for-Postcolonial},
