rdination Versus Initiation in Newar Buddhism (Jens-Uwe Hartmann), 23. The Original Buddha and the Recent Buddha: A Preliminary Report on Buddhism in a Gurung Community (Heinz Bechert) LITERATURE 24. Two Nepalese Versions of the Mahīrāvaṇa Tale (William L. Smith), 25. The Kṛṣṇacaritra - Some Observations on a Classical Nevārī Drama (Carl Suneson), ART AND ARCHITECTURE 26. Dhunge-Dhārās in the Kathmandu Valley - Continuity and Development of Architectural Design (Raimund O.A. Becker-Ritterspach), 27. Naikāp - A Settlement Determined by Newar Changes Its Sacred Forms (Reinhard Herdick), 28. Preliminary Notes on an India - Import Scroll from Nepal (Mary Shepherd Slusser) ETHNOMUSICOLOGY 29. The Mathematics of Newar Buddhist Music (Ter Ellingson), 30. Expression of Ethnicity and Politics in Bhajan Singing. Some Preliminary Results on the Assimilation of Modern Mediated Music in a Traditional Newar Community (Ingemar Grandin), 31. Urbanisation of Gurung Culture and Identity - A Study of Gurung Music in Kathmandu (Pirkko Moisala), 32. Music and Death - Sībājā of the Newar Butchers (Gert-Matthias Wegner).},
