  abstract         = {Mahābhāṣya Pradīpa Vyākhyānāni. Commentaires sur le Mahābhāṣya de Patañjali et le Pradīpa de Kaiyaṭa. Edition par M.S. Narasimhacharya. Présentation par Pierre- Sylvain Filliozat (dans vol. I). Introduction et index par M.S. Narasimhacharya (dans vol. X). Préface (au vol. X) par P.S. Filliozat. Vol. I : Adhyāya 1, Pāda 1, Āhnika 1-4, 1973, xxii, 397 p. Vol. II : Adhyāya 1, Pāda 1, Āhnika 5-7, 1975, 367 p. Vol. III : Adhyāya 1, Pāda 1, Āhnika 8-9, 1976, 315 p. Vol. IV : Adhyāya 1, Pāda 2-4, 1977, v, 383 p. Vol. V : Adhyāya 2, Pāda 1-4, 1978, vi, 379 p. Vol. VI : Adhyāya 3, Pāda 1-4, 1979, vi, 420 p. Vol. VII : Adhyāya 4, Pāda 1-4, 1980, vi, 398 p. Vol. VIII : Adhyāya 5, Pāda 1-4, 1981, 254 p. Vol. IX : Adhyāya 6, Pāda 1-4, 1982, 408 p. Vol. X : Adhyāya 7 et 8, 1983, cli, 503 p. (PIFI n°51) Language: Sanskrit. (French introd.)  Grammar in India can be equated with the study of Sanskrit (considered as Language par excellence), rigorous in research and description, and having attained the highest scientific level since antiquity. The interpretation of Pāṇini’s grammar following the guidelines defined by Patañjali is alive in traditional Sanskrit schools to this day. The Mahābhasya of Patañjali is a model of the art of reasoning and has been abundantly commented upon over the centuries. The present edition is intended to make available to readers all that has survived of these commentaries.},
