  annotation       = {p.405: mentions that A. K. Priyolkar, \emph{Damayantī-Svayaṃvara} (Aundh, Satara, Svadhyaya mandal, 1935), says, intro p.32, that ``many learned men from the \emph{Mahārāṣṭra} migrated to Tanjore after Shivaji's death in A.D.1680".\\ p.405 and n.3, Letter by Ramadasa to Raghunāthabhaṭa Gosāvī poublished by S. S. Dev \emph{Śrīsaṃpradāyācī Patreṃ} (Dhulia, 1915). Letter no.1 in green ink, in the hand-writing of Saint Rāmadāsa. It says `\emph{tuṃhī sarvajña āhā}" (Gode 408, no.1) \\p.405: ref to a list of pandits at the Tanjore court, 1643--1712, given in the intro. to \emph{Śabdaratnasamanvaya} (G.O. Series, Baroda). \\ The \emph{Prayogarathnabhūṣā} of Ragh. (MS 610 of the BBRAS) gives four generations of the family: Navahasta Hariharabhaṭṭa (c.AD 1600), son Raghunātha (c. AD 1600), son Gaṇeśabhaṭṭa (c. AD 1650), son Raghunātha (fl. AD 1640 -- 1710) \\ Ramadas's letters to Ragh. dated 1674. Other letters in S. S. Dev's book which mention Ragh are dated 1679, 1679 again, 1680, 1682, 1682, 1683 etc. through 1716. In the first one of 1682 (letter no.51), Ragh is mentioned as staying with Rāmadāsa during the latter's illness. In 1683, letters 55 and 56, Ragh. writes that he is going on pilgrimage and he is giving all his property and land holdings, including land granted to him by Rāmadāsa (an inām at Bilāśī), to his son in law Bhairavabhaṭa Mahābaleśvarakara. Letter 138 of 1702 mentions R's pilgrimage to Varanasi. \\ Gode p.412: Raghunatha residing at Chafal in 1679. He had been upādhyāya and purāṇīka since 1648 when the temple of Śrīraghupati was built there. Shivaji came to Chafal and met Rāmadāsa there in 1649. \\ p.413: death of Shivaji in 1680. D. of Rāmadāsa in 1682 . 1683, Ragh decides to go to Benares. Death of Ekoji in same year? 1684--1712, rule of Shahaji in Tanjore. Many pandits gather at Tanjore during his reign. Ragh is there, patronised by Dipabai.},
  modificationdate = {2019-01-12T00:00:00},
  owner            = {dom},
  source           = {CUL 834.01.b.6.38},
}

