  abstract   = {Mentions Dhank three times. P.48-49 contain the following story, \begin{quote}Vanthali was for a long time known by the name of Patan, but Vahudipal Dhundhlimal the Yogi, who lived in the hills of Dhank, in his wrath pronounced the curse "\emph{Patan so datan!}" "Patan, be buried!" upon it; whereupon eighty-four towns bearing that name were swallowed up by the earth, and Patan shared the same fate, as may be seen even in our days, since, where-ever excavations are made, foundations of buildings, and various things, are dug up.  During the tenure of power of the author in this town, two stone horses, each one cubit high, were ducg up, with a stone box in which they were, and also other more valuable things in Saṃvat 1842 (A.D. 1785).\end{quote}},
  translator = {E. Rehatsek},
}

