  annotation       = {From the notes in the Vienna Nbh-MSS-Concordance: "Remarks: The list in this printed booklet was compiled by Rajaram Shastri of Kashmir. Before the list of contents, it is stated on p. 47: likhitaṃ paṇḍitarājārāmaśāstriṇā kāśmīravāsinā. The booklet is not dated and bears no reference to the collection it relates to, nor to any place of publication. The list is tentatively assigned to 1880 in ABC, to approximately 1870 in the SB copy, and to approximately 1881 in the TUUB copy. The connection to the collection of Radhakrishna of Lahore is made in the CC and in a hand-written note on the title page of the copy of the SB. In the ABC, a connection is made to the collection of Maharaja Digvijay Singh of Balrampur, probably on the basis of a hand-written note on the IOL copy. Balrampur is also mentioned in the catalogue of the TUUB as the place of publication of its copy."},
